			<div class="content" id="post-content-2408721">
									

<p>+1</p>
<p>I almost downvoted because, well, it's an amp that's just really good at being an amp. Looking at the <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/the-big-list-of-overdone-scp-cliches">The Big List of Cliches</a>, we see that comes in at #11. [Crank it up to 11!] There's just not much of a hook, and the Demon thing feels a little tacked-on.</p>
<p>I upvoted because its obvious you put a metric shit-tonne of work into this thing, and, as a technical writer myself, its probably the most technically detailed article I've seen on the wiki. And that made it feel <strong>real</strong>. It's a testament to clinical tone and attention to detail. <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">I probably wouldn't read it again, but</span> I think it is something that can belong on the site and flesh out the Foundation universe a little bit better. It feels like something the Foundation would <em>actually have</em> in their database files somewhere. Again, it feels <strong>real.</strong></p>

							</div>

								
